<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Uda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/866">866</a>–931</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Uda-tennō, Sadami, Minamoto no Sadami</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Uda was the 59th emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> according to the traditional order of succession, reigning from 887 to 897. A son of Emperor Kōkō, he had been demoted to commoner status as Minamoto no Sadami in 884 and was restored as an imperial prince only in 887, just before his father's death. His attempt in the Akō controversy to make the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujiwara-no-mototsune">Fujiwara no Mototsune</a>'s office merely honorific failed, and only after Mototsune died in 891 could he rule directly, promoting men outside the main Fujiwara line such as Sugawara no Michizane and ending missions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>. He abdicated in 897 in favour of his son Daigo, became a monk and died in 931.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-uda.jpg" alt="Emperor Uda" width="330" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown; derivative work by bamse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Uda_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>An emperor born of another mother could slip their hold: <b>Emperor Uda</b> regained much of the government, and Emperor Go-Sanjō, from 1068, curbed the Fujiwara and began the rule of retired emperors.</blockquote><a href="/societies/heian-japan">Social Hierarchy of Heian Japan</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heian-kyo">Heian-kyō</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. Died in Ninna-ji Temple, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35,135.77&amp;year=908" aria-label="Heian-kyō on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7991 898 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Emperor Uda"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8441 1168h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8441 1168h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=35,135.77&amp;year=908">What was here in 908 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
